! jb_ax4b "IBOX-4", routine 1244 ("RENAME CHECK"), TEST 4 -- the
! driver at labels I4412-I4422, PDF pp.90-91, octal
! 006470.00-006523.40, plus the two data words that close the routine
! (006524.00-006525.00) and the "-CONSTANTS FOR 1244." block on PDF
! p.98 (006726.00-006735.00).  56 half-words of code, 10 full words of
! data.
!
! CITED BY PDF PAGE, AND THAT IS A CORRECTION.  The brief for this
! transcription said jb_ax4b's listing carries printed page numbers and
! asked for the printed-to-PDF offset.  It does not.  Page 90 was
! rendered at 300 dpi and its top strip, bottom strip, left edge and
! right edge were all read: there is no folio anywhere on the sheet,
! and the front write-up carries none either.  What settles which pages
! to read is content, and it agrees at offset ZERO with every number
! the repo already uses for this deck:
!     PDF p.85   the 1244 header, "----1244---RENAME CHECK."
!     PDF p.90   this block, "-TEST 4." and labels I4412-I4422
!     PDF p.93   error table 1, entries 11 through 21
!     PDF p.190  I00Z at 013034.00 and I00VO at 013036.00, which
!                programs/ibox4_refill_nop.strap already cites as
!                "common constants (p.190)"
! So "p.NN" for jb_ax4b means the PDF's own page, exactly as it already
! did in verify_ibox4_listing.py and the ibox4_cb*/refill programs.
! The offset is 0 because there is nothing to offset FROM.
!
! WHY THIS BLOCK MATTERS.  Routine 1244's header (PDF p.85) lists four
! things the test checks.  Item 4, verbatim:
!
!     -4. CHECK THAT THE INSTRUCTION IS
!         -NO OPPED WHEN EITHER THE
!         -OLD OR THE NEW REFILL FIELD
!         -OF IX REG 0 LIES IN THE
!         -RANGE OF 1 TO 37 OCTAL.
!
! That is a SECOND refill-address no-op rule, and its range is NOT the
! one routine 1238 establishes for R/RCZ.  1238's header says "NOPING
! IF RF IS FROM 1 TO 15" and its test 2 pins that boundary from both
! sides (programs/ibox4_refill_nop.strap: word 0 DOES refill, words
! 1-15 do not).  1244 says 1 to 37 OCTAL -- 1 to 31 decimal -- for RNX.
! Two instructions, two ranges, in the same deck.  Whatever the rule
! for one is, it is not automatically the rule for the other, and this
! block is the affirmative evidence that says so.
!
! The Reference Manual agrees that RNX's range is the wider one, and
! disagrees with the deck about the bottom end.  22-6530-2, printed
! p.27 (PDF p.30 -- the footer reads "Operand Designation  27", and the
! +3 offset is the one ax5b_162_test3a.strap already records for this
! manual), section "Rename (RNX)", read first-hand at 150 dpi:
!
!     "The index word in the index register specified by the field J is
!     stored in the location addressed by the refill field of X0.  The
!     refill field of X0 is then replaced by bits 0-17 of the effective
!     address.  The remaining bits of X0 remain unchanged.  Next, the
!     index word specified by J is replaced by the word in core storage
!     addressed by the new refill field of X0.  When either the old or
!     the new name of the index refers to one of the locations 0-31,
!     the instruction is executed as no-operation and indicator AD is
!     set."
!
! Manual: 0-31.  Deck header: 1 to 37 octal.  And that same paragraph
! is why TEST 4 comes in two halves: the OLD name is index 0's refill
! field, which I4414-I4416 sets with the patched "LRI,$X0,0.0"; the NEW
! name is "bits 0-17 of the effective address", which I4417-I4419
! supplies through the patched "RNX,$X1,I4418".  One error table each,
! and the tables' own words -- "IX 0 INITIAL REFILL ADDRESS" and
! "EFFECTIVE ADDRESS" -- are the manual's two names.
!
! THE SAME PAGE SETTLES THE FIELD BOUNDARY the RNX rows below depend
! on.  Immediately above that paragraph the manual prints RENAME's
! format, and its tick marks read: ADDRESS 0, J 19, OP. 23, I 28, 31.
! So the direct-index operation code is bits 23-27 -- five bits
! straddling the printed octal pair and the printed hex byte -- which
! is exactly how the two RNX rows and their LX neighbour decompose.
! Not inferred from two samples; printed in the manual.
!
! AND THE DECK KNOWS.  PDF p.98's constants block is the tell, and it
! is the best thing on these pages:
!
!     I44XW1  XW,I44B1,0,0        6530.00 00 000000.00 00   006730.00
!     I44XW2  XW,I44B2,0,0        6630.00 00 000000.00 00   006731.00
!     I44XW3  XW,1.0,31,0            1.00 00 000760.00 00   006732.00
!             -IF 0 BECOMES ILLEGAL FOR RNX, USE THE
!             -FOLLOWING THREE INDEX WORDS TO REPLACE
!             -THOSE DIRECTLY ABOVE.
!     I44XWA  XW,I44B1A,0,0       6526.00 00 000000.00 00   006733.00
!     I44XWB  XW,I44B2A,0,0       6626.00 00 000000.00 00   006734.00
!     I44XWC  XW,0.0,32,0            0.00 00 001000.00 00   006735.00
!
! As shipped the loop starts at address 1.0 with a count of 31 and
! walks 1 through 37 octal, matching the routine header.  A spare set
! sits beside it, starting at 0.0 with a count of 32 and pointing at
! the "ADDRESS IS 0." entries of both error tables, ready to be swapped
! in "IF 0 BECOMES ILLEGAL FOR RNX" -- i.e. if the machine turns out to
! behave the way the Reference Manual's "0-31" says.  The boundary at
! zero was an OPEN question to the people who wrote this test, and they
! left the patch in the deck rather than pick a side.  Both index-word
! triples are transcribed below; only the first is the one the driver
! loads.
!
! BOTH ERROR TABLES ARE PRINTED ON THESE PAGES and their text is the
! contract.  Read first-hand at 100 dpi on PDF pp.92-94 (table 1) and
! pp.95-97 (table 2):
!
!     -ERROR BRANCH TABLE 1.
!     -YOU CAME TO THIS ERROR TABLE FROM I4416
!   I44B1A  SIC,SEN   -RNX FAILS TO NOP WHEN IX 0 INITIAL REFILL
!           B,SERS    -ADDRESS IS 0.
!           V+I,$X10,1.0
!           B,I4417
!   I44B1   ... -ADDRESS IS 1. ... through -ADDRESS IS 31.
!
!     -ERROR BRANCH TABLE 2.
!     -YOU CAME TO THIS ERROR TABLE FROM I4419
!   I44B2A  SIC,SEN   -RNX FAILS TO NOP WHEN EFFECTIVE
!           B,SERS    -ADDRESS IS 0.
!           V+I,$X10,1.0
!           B,I4420
!   I44B2   ... -ADDRESS IS 1. ... through -ADDRESS IS 31.
!
! Each table is 32 entries of 2 words: table 1 at 006526.00-006625.40,
! table 2 at 006626.00-006725.40.  Note the shape of an entry -- it
! reports, bumps $X10 (the error counter) and BRANCHES BACK INTO THE
! LOOP, at I4417 for table 1 and I4420 for table 2.  A failure does not
! stop the test; it is counted and the walk continues.
!
! THE TABLES ARE STUBBED HERE, not transcribed.  Sixty-four entries of
! four identical half-words apiece would add nothing this file does not
! already check, so each table gets eight bare "BEW, $" halts at its
! own address -- enough to define I44B1A/I44B1 and I44B2A/I44B2 for the
! index words above, and to stop a wrong branch instead of letting it
! run on.  This is what programs/ibox4_refill_nop.strap does with
! 1238's table at 005674.00.  Entries 2 through 31 of each table are
! NOT transcribed and are NOT checked.
!
! HOW TEST 4 WORKS, row by row, because it is self-modifying in two
! different ways at once.
!
!   I4412 SETUP.  $X15 <- I44XW1 (value -> error table 1), $X14 <-
!   I44XW2 (value -> error table 2), $X12 <- I44XW3 (value 1.0, count
!   31).  $X11 <- count 10.  $X10 <- 0, the error counter.
!
!   I4413 THE FOUR SVAs.  "Store Value in Address" writes an index
!   register's VALUE into the ADDRESS FIELD of an instruction further
!   down, and all four targets are in this block:
!       SVA,$X15,I4416   the "$B,0" that jumps into error table 1
!       SVA,$X14,I4419   the "$B,0" that jumps into error table 2
!       SVA,$X12,I4415   the "LRI,$X0,0.0" that sets the OLD refill
!       SVA,$X12,I4418   the "RNX,$X1,I4418" -- ITS OWN ADDRESS FIELD
!   So each pass round the loop the two error-table branches are aimed
!   at the entry for the address being tried, and the address being
!   tried is planted twice: once as index 0's refill field, once as
!   RNX's effective address.  The same trick 1238's test 2H uses for
!   its two patched fields, here with four.
!
!   I4414 FIRST HALF -- THE OLD REFILL.  Zero $X1, give it a count of
!   777777 octal, clear I44D1, load the all-ones index word I00VO into
!   $X2 and store it at I44D2.  "LRI,$X0,0.0" (address field patched)
!   puts the trial address into index 0's REFILL field.  Then
!   "RNX,$X1,I44D2": rename index 1 from I44D2.  If RNX no-ops as it
!   should, $X1 is untouched; "LX,$X1,$X1 / BXVZ,$+1.0" skips the error
!   when the index VALUE is zero, and "$B,0" reports when it is not.
!   The trailing "BXCZ,I4416" is the loop's own guard.
!
!   I4417 SECOND HALF -- THE NEW REFILL.  The same preparation, but
!   "LRI,$X0,I44D2" gives index 0 a LEGAL old refill and the patched
!   "RNX,$X1,I4418" supplies the trial address as the EFFECTIVE
!   address, i.e. the NEW name.  "LX,$X1,I44D2 / BXVZ,I4419" reports
!   through table 2 if the rename happened.
!
!   I4420-I4421 THE WALK.  "LX,$X10,$X10 / BZXVZ,I4421" tests the error
!   counter and, when it is non-zero, skips straight on to the next
!   address ("-TO NEXT ADDRESS" is the listing's own comment on that
!   row).  Otherwise "C-I,$X11,1 / BXCZ,$+1.0 / BD,I4414" repeats the
!   pass ten times at the same address ("-NO ERROR, CONTINUE.").  Then
!   $X12 counts the 31 addresses down, bumping its value by 1.0 and
!   both table pointers by 2.0 -- two words, exactly one table entry --
!   before branching back to I4413 to re-aim all four SVAs.
!
!   I4422 THE EXIT.  "B,$+1.0 / BD,I4412" is the deck's re-entry hook,
!   then "SIC,SENO+.32 / B,SSW" hands off to SSIP and the continuity
!   register IC244 is updated and checked against ICK244.
!
! THE ENCODING ORACLE, AND RNX'S FIRST LISTING WITNESS.  RNX has never
! been witnessed by a printed listing in this repo: no verify_*.py
! contains an RNX row.  The name does appear four other places, and
! none of them is a transcribed instruction -- opcodes.py's table
! entry, audit_opcode_coverage.py's coverage list, a COMMENT in
! programs/ibox4_refill_nop.strap noting that ja_ax1a's constants print
! "$RNX" as a patchable constant WORD (a datum, never transcribed), and
! a COMMENT in programs/problem_2_2_method3.strap recording that bsv
! does not implement it.  These two rows are the first,
!     006477.40  RNX,$X1,I44D2   6727.03 F0
!     006505.00  RNX,$X1,I4418   6505.03 F0
! and they pin the 5-bit direct-index code: bit 23 plus bits 24-27 read
! 1 1111 = 0b11111, exactly DIR_INDEX_CODES["RNX"].  (The brief said
! RNX was in MISC_CODES; it is not -- it is in DIR_INDEX_CODES, the
! same table as LX/SX/SVA, and the encoding above is why.)
!
! ENCODING ONLY, and RNX is the reason it could not be otherwise.
! bsv/StretchDecode.bsv does define dixop_RNX = 5'b11111 and
! StretchTypes.bsv names it, so the word DECODES; but
! StretchExecute.bsv:2693 falls through to "default: ind =
! setOpInvalid(ind); // RNX, LVE: out of scope", so the model executes
! it as Operation Code Invalid.  StretchSmoke.bsv even uses RNX as its
! deliberate "structurally-valid opcode" that sets OP.  There is
! nothing to run here; what a listing can settle is the BIT PATTERN,
! and that is what verify_ibox4_rnx_nop_listing.py settles.
!
! SUBSTITUTIONS: three, all mechanical.
!   1. Digit-leading labels take an "L" prefix -- L14412..L14422,
!      L144B1, L144B1A, L144B2, L144B2A, L144D1, L144D2, L144XW1..3,
!      L144XWA..C, L146 -- the convention ax5b_162_test3a.strap and
!      ax5b_162_exic_classes.strap already use.
!   2. The listing's "$B,0" at I4416 and I4419 is written "B, 0".  The
!      dollar prefix is the deck's mark for an opcode assembled as a
!      patchable word (ja_ax1a's "$L%BU" and "$RNX"; 1238's I3825 does
!      the same thing at 005537.00).  It changes no bit: the printed
!      code is 0.10 00, a plain B to address 0.
!   3. The octal marker "%8@" is written "(8)": "%8@777777" ->
!      "(8)777777", "%8@740000.00" -> "(8)740000.0".  Load-bearing, not
!      decoration -- the listing's default radix is decimal (see
!      "LCI,$X11,10", which prints 12.27 02, i.e. ten in bits 0-17) and
!      so is this assembler's, so an unmarked 777777 would assemble as
!      decimal.  The same point ax5b_162_test3a.strap makes about
!      "(8)3740".
!
! EXTERNALS, SYN'd at the addresses this same listing prints.  THESE
! ARE INPUTS TO THE CHECK, NOT WITNESSES -- the caveat
! verify_ax5b_16082_16083_listing.py makes about I6088.  A SYN row
! MAKES the address field come out right, so a row naming one proves
! only that every OTHER field lands where the listing puts it.  Two of
! the seven have a second, independently read page behind them (I00VO
! from PDF p.190's own label column, BIT3 from PDF p.191's); that is
! corroboration, and corroboration still does not turn an input into a
! witness.  The rest rest on other verify files in this repo.
!
! Transcription standard: bit-exact against the printed machine code,
! verify_ibox4_rnx_nop_listing.py.

SEN     SYN, (8)1310.0        ! the SIC error-entry link
SENO    SYN, (8)1311.0        ! PDF p.190's own label column: "SENO"
SERS    SYN, (8)1304.0        ! the error-report routine
SSW     SYN, (8)1301.0        ! the SSIP return
I00VO   SYN, (8)13036.0       ! indx wd. of ones, PDF p.190
BIT3    SYN, (8)13057.0       ! XW,%8@40000.00,0,0 -- PDF p.191
I46    SYN, (8)6736.0        ! the next routine; address from this operand

! -- TEST 4, the driver.  PDF p.90, 006470.00-006521.40. -------------
        SLC, (8)6470.0
I4412  LX,  $X15, I44XW1            ! -SETUP
        LX,  $X14, I44XW2
        LX,  $X12, I44XW3
I4413  SVA, $X15, I4416             ! aim error table 1's branch
        SVA, $X14, I4419             ! aim error table 2's branch
        SVA, $X12, I4415             ! plant the trial OLD refill
        SVA, $X12, I4418             ! plant the trial EFFECTIVE address
        LCI, $X11, 10                 ! decimal ten -- prints 12.27 02
        Z,   $X10                     ! the error counter

I4414  Z,   $X1                      ! -START TEST.
        LCI, $X1, (8)777777
        Z,   I44D1
        LX,  $X2, I00VO
        SX,  $X2, I44D2
I4415  LRI, $X0, 0.0                 ! address field patched by I4413
        RNX, $X1, I44D2              ! old refill in range -> must no-op
        LX,  $X1, $X1
        BXVZ, $+1.0
I4416  B,   0                        ! listing "$B,0" -BRANCH TO ERROR TABLE 1.
        BXCZ, I4416

I4417  Z,   $X1
        LCI, $X1, (8)777777
        Z,   I44D1
        LX,  $X2, I00VO
        SX,  $X2, I44D2
        LRI, $X0, I44D2              ! a LEGAL old refill this time
I4418  RNX, $X1, I4418              ! its own address field, patched
        LX,  $X1, I44D2
        BXVZ, I4419
        BXCZ, I4420
I4419  B,   0                        ! listing "$B,0" -BRANCH TO ERROR TABLE 2.

I4420  LX,  $X10, $X10
        BZXVZ, I4421                 ! -TO NEXT ADDRESS

        C-I, $X11, 1                  ! -NO ERROR, CONTINUE.
        BXCZ, $+1.0
        BD,  I4414

I4421  C-I, $X12, 1
        BXCZ, I4422
        V+I, $X12, 1.0                ! next trial address
        V+I, $X14, 2.0                ! next table 2 entry (two words)
        V+I, $X15, 2.0                ! next table 1 entry
        B,   I4413

I4422  B,   $+1.0
        BD,  I4412
        SIC, SENO+.32
        B,   SSW                      ! -TO SSIP
        BD,  $+.32

        LX,  $X13, IC244              ! -UPDATE CONTINUITY CHECK.
        V+,  $X13, BIT3
        SX,  $X13, IC244

        LX,  $X13, IC244              ! -UPDATE CONTINUITY CHECK.
        KV,  $X13, ICK244
! -- PDF p.91, 006522.00-006525.00 -----------------------------------
        SIC, SEN
        BZXE, SERS                    ! -CONTINUITY ERROR.
        B,   I46
        CNOP                          ! prints 0.30 00 at 006523.40
IC244   XW, 0, 0, 0                   ! -CONTINUITY REG 1244.
ICK244  XW, (8)740000.0, 0, 0

! -- ERROR BRANCH TABLE 1, STUBBED.  32 entries of 2 words, 006526.00
! -- through 006625.40; only the first two are given, as bare halts at
! -- their own addresses, so a wrong branch stops instead of running
! -- on.  Their text is quoted in the header.  I44B1A is an ANCHOR,
! -- not evidence: the SLC below puts the counter there, from the
! -- address column of PDF p.92, so I44XWA printing 6526.00 checks this
! -- transcription against its own SLC -- the same status I4412 has.
! -- I44B1 is one step better only in that four stub half-words have
! -- to be sized right for it to land.
        SLC, (8)6526.0
I44B1A BEW, $                        ! -ADDRESS IS 0.
        BEW, $
        BEW, $
        BEW, $
I44B1  BEW, $                        ! -ADDRESS IS 1.
        BEW, $
        BEW, $
        BEW, $

! -- ERROR BRANCH TABLE 2, STUBBED the same way.  32 entries of 2
! -- words, 006626.00 through 006725.40.
        SLC, (8)6626.0
I44B2A BEW, $                        ! -ADDRESS IS 0.
        BEW, $
        BEW, $
        BEW, $
I44B2  BEW, $                        ! -ADDRESS IS 1.
        BEW, $
        BEW, $
        BEW, $

! -- "-CONSTANTS FOR 1244.", PDF p.98, 006726.00-006735.00 -----------
        SLC, (8)6726.0
I44D1  XW, 0, 0, 0
I44D2  XW, 0, 0, 0
I44XW1 XW, I44B1,  0, 0             ! -> error table 1, entry "1"
I44XW2 XW, I44B2,  0, 0             ! -> error table 2, entry "1"
I44XW3 XW, 1.0, 31, 0                ! start at 1.0, walk 31 addresses
!       -IF 0 BECOMES ILLEGAL FOR RNX, USE THE
!       -FOLLOWING THREE INDEX WORDS TO REPLACE
!       -THOSE DIRECTLY ABOVE.
I44XWA XW, I44B1A, 0, 0             ! -> error table 1, entry "0"
I44XWB XW, I44B2A, 0, 0             ! -> error table 2, entry "0"
I44XWC XW, 0.0, 32, 0                ! start at 0.0, walk 32 addresses
        END, I4412
